A||||1||Michael||Braking power?||||5||
Z||000000||Michael||09-05-2000||07:21 AM||||Are those cross drilled rotors worth putting on my 85GT?  I`m going to do some engine work later on, so I might need some exrta broking power.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||09-05-2000||07:40 AM||||From what I have heard on the subject, FWIW, drilled rotors are 99% cosmetic. Sure,if you are racing on a road course, you may exerience some fade with repetitve high speed braking, which is where the drilled rotors will come into play.  But if you are looking for more serious grippage in a panic stop situation then those little holes add nothing to the equation.<BR>   If you want to improve your stopping power, I would suggest first stainless braided lines as old rubber fiero lines have a tendency to balloon, decreasing braking power. Then you may want to try Baretta/Grand Am brake conversion. If that's still not enough for you, there is a nifty Brembo kit available with 12" rotors (cross drilled for your comfort) 4 piston calipers, your cost? Oh about $2700!<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
